            <div xml:id="d749">

                <pb facs="0847" n="837" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg837"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.6336/11–1848: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-18">November 18,
                        1948</date>.<lb/>[Received November 18—4:40 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2464. Following received from Mukden, 4 p. m., 18th:</p>
                <p>“Mukden radio station now closing down and will not reopen as it is in process
                    being seized. Inform Department, Embassy soonest. Ward.”</p>
                <p>Sent Department 2464; repeated Nanking 1863.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
